{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrvxL1kmJan1rpB1haWM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented `jsonpatch/core.py` per the spec and added `tests/test_core.py`. All 37 tests pass with `python3 -m unittest`.\n\n**Implementation notes:**\n- **Pointer resolution:** `resolve_pointer` splits and unescapes tokens (`~1` before `~0`). It rejects leading zeros, `-`, out-of-range indices, invalid `~` escapes, and descent into scalars, all as `PointerError`.\n- **Atomicity:** `apply_patch` applies every operation to a deep copy of the input. If any operation fails, the input is never touched. With `in_place=True`, the input is updated only after all operations succeed.\n- **Aliasing:** `value` payloads are deep-copied, so later operations can't mutate the caller's patch dict.\n\n**Choices the spec didn't settle:**\n- `remove` on the root (`\"\"`) raises `PatchError`. The spec doesn't say what should happen, so I chose to disallow it.\n- `move` checks the \"own child\" rule by path tokens, not string prefixes. So `/a` → `/ab/x` is allowed.\n- `test` on a missing path raises `PointerError`, which is a `PatchError` subclass.\n- With `in_place=True` and a scalar root replaced, there is nothing to mutate, so the new value is returned.\n\nI did not commit anything, and I did not run `pytest` (the tests are written to work under either runner)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17310,"cache_read_input_tokens":33979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17310},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"763daa63-9470-4625-91d7-027fd9108348","uuid":"ba4c3170-86dc-4c2c-ab3c-798f6cacc3d5","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:52:06.890Z","reque